ccsd has been offering free breakfast  and lunch to children at all at schools  across the county but it appears very  few kids are showing up jeremy j ford  joining us live in the newsroom right  now to share what he found out after he  visited several campuses today jeremy  well on tuesday the school district  kicked off its summer food program  providing free in-person meals for  children but turnout appears to be just  a little bit low  i stopped at several schools this  afternoon during lunch  and although it's just three days in i'm  told by some school staff children are  not showing up to eat in the cafeteria  besides the students there for summer  classes i spoke with ccsd communications  manager mauricio marin he explains why  this year the district doesn't have  grab-and-go meals the meals are meant  here to be consumed in our air  conditioned facility and that's to  comply with the guidelines that we get  from the usda now some school staff tell  me they would prefer kids to have the  option to stop by and pick up meals  earlier i reached out on facebook live  asking parents if they're allowing their  kids to eat breakfast or dinner in  person and the majority responded they  would prefer to grab and go while some  parents didn't even know their kids  could eat for free  now i've reached out again to the school  district to see if this would be an  option or if it's going to remain an  in-school option i'm waiting to hear  back and we've also listed the schools  participating in the program and you can  find them on eight 8newsnow.com  reporting from the newsroom jeremy j  ford live  local now
 

